# 🖨️ Printing Integration — Bluetooth (ESC/POS) + Trendit / Topwise Built-in SDKs

How receipt printing works in this app, and what to copy over when porting the
feature into another Flutter project.

---

## 1. Overview

The app can print a receipt three ways, and the user picks which one(s) to use
from **Printer Settings**:

| Backend | Used when | Talks to |
|---|---|---|
| **Built-in printer — Trendit** | Device is a Trendit POS terminal | `com.trendit.basesdk.device.printer.*` (native Android SDK, bundled as a `.jar`) |
| **Built-in printer — Topwise** | Device is a Topwise POS terminal | `com.topwise.cloudpos.aidl.printer.*` (native Android SDK via AIDL, bundled as a `.jar`) |
| **External Bluetooth printer** | Any external ESC/POS thermal printer, on any device | `print_bluetooth_thermal` + `esc_pos_utils_plus` (pure Dart/Flutter plugin, no native SDK) |

The two built-in SDKs are mutually exclusive per physical device (a terminal
is either Trendit or Topwise hardware), so the native Android code detects
which SDK is actually available at runtime and routes to the right one. The
Bluetooth path is entirely separate — it's a generic ESC/POS implementation
that works on any phone/tablet paired with any thermal printer, independent
of which POS hardware (or none) the app is running on.

### Data flow

```
Flutter (Dart)                                   Android (native)
───────────────                                   ─────────────────
PrinterDispatch.run(...)
   │
   ├── printBuiltin() ──► PrintHelper.printReceipt()
   │                         │  (MethodChannel: com.geepay.pos_mobile/print)
   │                         ▼
   │                     MainActivity's channel handler
   │                         │
   │                         ├─ TopwisePrinterHelper.getPrinterIfAvailable()
   │                         │     found? ──► TopwisePrinterHelper.printReceipt(...)
   │                         │
   │                         └─ not found ──► falls through to the existing
   │                                          inline Trendit `printerDevice` code
   │                                          in MainActivity.java
   │
   └── printBluetooth() ──► BluetoothPrinterHelper.printReceipt()
                                │ (pure Dart, esc_pos_utils_plus + print_bluetooth_thermal)
                                ▼
                            PrintBluetoothThermal.writeBytes(...)  → paired BT printer
```

`PrinterDispatch` + `PrinterPreference` decide **which** backend(s) a call site
uses; each backend's actual printing code is otherwise unaware of the other.

