## 4. Built-in printer — Topwise SDK (native Android, AIDL)

Topwise terminals expose printing via `AidlPrinter`, obtained from
`DeviceServiceManager` (Topwise's `TOPUSDK`/`cloudpos` AIDL service). This was
added **without touching** the existing Trendit code path — `MainActivity`
tries Topwise first and falls back to the inline Trendit code if unavailable.

**Files to copy:**
- `android/app/src/main/java/com/example/pos_mobile/TopwisePrinterHelper.java`
  (full code below) — self-contained: builds a `PrintTemplate` (business
  name, fields, divider, logo) and renders it as a bitmap via
  `AidlPrinter.addRuiImage` / `printRuiQueue`.
- In `MainActivity.java`: the `TopwisePrinterHelper.getPrinterIfAvailable()`
  check at the top of each of `printReceipt` / `printZescoReceipt` /
  `printDailySummary`, and the `import com.topwise.cloudpos.aidl.printer.AidlPrinter;`
  import (see full `MainActivity.java` glue in section 5 below).
- The Topwise SDK jar: `android/app/libs/topwise/T1_V2_20260326.jar`
  (device/firmware-specific — get the matching jar for the target Topwise
  model/SDK version from Topwise).
- `R.drawable.logo` — same drawable resource the Trendit/Bluetooth paths use
  for the receipt logo; make sure it exists in the target project's
  `android/app/src/main/res/drawable/`.
- Reference docs/demo (not code to ship, just for API reference when
